{#- Shared frontmatter fields — included by all SKILL.md.j2 templates.
   Place between the opening --- and closing --- of the YAML frontmatter.

   `skill_tools` is the harness-native tool list the skill pre-approves on
   Claude. It defaults to the writing set the authoring skills need; a skill
   that writes nothing sets a narrower list with `{% set %}` before the include
   (box M of `wip/plugin-skills-gaps/design.md`). The field pre-approves, it
   does not restrict — an unlisted tool is still callable and simply asks
   first — so a narrow list is what makes a write in a read-only skill stop for
   the user rather than what makes it impossible.

   MCP tools are never listed here: their names are per-platform, so each skill
   appends its own after the include. -#}
{% if platform == "claude" -%}
allowed-tools:
{%- for tool in skill_tools | default(["Bash", "Read", "Write", "Edit", "Grep", "Glob"]) %}
  - {{ tool }}
{%- endfor %}
{% endif -%}
